# Events for the automatic run of widget_test: see doc/auto_events.md.
#
# The mouse and key lines go in at the display's seat, as a person's would.
# A point is in the client area of the main window. The points are those of
# GNOME over Wayland, read off the screens of its standard,
# tests/compare/linux/gnome/wayland/widget_test.cmp; another desktop or
# backend lays its widgets out to its own sizes and wants a file of its own.
#
# Each line is a step of its frame, and the screen after it is captured: a
# press is three, the move to the point, the button down and the button up.
# A chapter's presses end with one at 700,600, on the main window, which
# takes the keyboard focus back from the widget pressed last, so that the
# return after it reaches the test and ends the chapter.
#
# The frames with no block here, the group boxes, the backgrounds and the
# dialogs, take no events.

# The real joystick is set aside; the keyboard and mouse are the file's
joystickoff

# Terminal buttons test: each button pressed, then the main window to
# take the focus back for the return; then again with the middle button
# disabled, which does nothing
sync 2
moumovg 1 281 252
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
moumovg 1 229 360
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
moumovg 1 221 468
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
moumovg 1 700 600
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
enter
moumovg 1 281 252
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
moumovg 1 229 360
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
moumovg 1 221 468
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
moumovg 1 700 600
mouba 1 1
moubd 1 1
enter

